LearnChemE, University of Colorado Boulder and contributing educators. [Official self-study modules](https://learncheme.com/quiz-yourself/interactive-self-study-modules/) · [Resources by course](https://learncheme.com/course-overview/).

Work the complete named material/energy-balance, phase-equilibrium, kinetics/reactor, separation and heat-transfer module sequences used in this study. They combine explanations, questions, examples and interactive demonstrations. Use an independently derived result to test each relevant demonstration; a simulation's animation is not experimental validation.

The publisher's module index, including recycle/purge, reactive and transient balances, flash separation, phase relations and heat accounts, was inspected on 29 October 2026. This is a collection of supporting teaching tools, not a replacement for complete textbooks or technical methods. Check each component's actual licence and software requirements; no blanket permission or successful interaction/playback is inferred from the index. All tools/media remain external.

